A||||22||batboy||Batmobile's 400 mile road trip||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||05-22-2000||05:02 PM||||I went caving and camping this last weekend. I've worked so hard and so much on the Batmobile, that I decided to drive it. Even though I took my entire toolbox (to be prepared), the Batmobile was well behaved. We had a fun adventure. The deep sounding throb of a V8 dual exhaust kept a grin on my face all weekend. I was hitting hard curves faster than ever. Almost all my friends demanded that I take them for a ride in my little "gokart".<P>I ran it up to 100 mph several times. No faster until I get new tires. I discovered that the power peak for my stock 350 V8 was between 2,500 and 4,500 rpm. I also found out that this rpm range (when cruising in top gear) corresponded with about 60 to 100+ mph. From 0-60 mph, a couple of the guys were a little disappointed, but from 60 to 100 mph the comments ranged from "awesome" to "terrifying" to "unbelieveable".<P>We camped at beautiful Lake Wilson in the north central Smoky Hills of Kansas. Plenty of hills and curves to test out my little Batmobile. I'd cruise up a steep grade and give it a little extra gas...the exhaust music would deepen to a lower note and the volume would slightly increase, then my Batmobile would effortlessly squirt up the hill and glide down the other side.<P>I was one with the car. My favorite music CD's playing on the stereo. The windows down and the sunroof off, the wind whipping through the car. Rough gravel roads were not much fun though. The suspension was a bit too stiff and low. But on the open two lane roads, I was passing anything and everything on the highway at will. One of my friends told me, "Your Fiero sounds tightly wound up." Punching it at 70 mph causes it to leap up to 90 mph almost instantly. <B>I HAD A BLAST!</B><P>Here's a pic of the Batmobile posed next to a Kansas wheat field (see below).<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 05-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-22-2000||05:33 PM||||Congrats!  I know you've been working pretty hard on it for a while now.  The feeling of accomplishment should be worth it all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/batMay2000_1.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 05-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||05-22-2000||05:34 PM||||I thought that the biggest hills in Kansas were the highway overpasses.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sluppy123||05-22-2000||05:37 PM||||Batboy -where's the chin spoiler????????||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||05-22-2000||07:59 PM||||Thanks for helping edit my pic, Monkey. Kansas don't have a lot of hills, but we have a few can actually be called hills. Sluppy, have patience, dude. I just now got it back on the road for the first time in months. I want to make sure it's reliable, which it seems to be so far. Next comes the body mods, like a wing, front air dam, hood louvers, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000005||dman||05-22-2000||08:10 PM||||Awesome batboy! Its been quite fun watching the progress of your batmobile over the past few months. My own projects seem to move at a snails pace so hearing about your 400 mile trip is great encouragement. Continued success and fun for your V8 fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||05-22-2000||08:27 PM||||Oh yeah! <B>TIRES!</B> I need tires and wheels...bad! Those crappy mismatched half wore out hunks of rubber that I'm currently calling tires need immediate replacing.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula||05-22-2000||09:05 PM||||Does the batmobile have a new 350 in it or is it the one that came factory?<P>jk, is that the high po 350 you mentioned earlier is this the orginal one that you got with the car?||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||05-22-2000||11:27 PM||||I have a 88 Z-28 350 roller engine that ought to crank out over 400 ponies that is planned to eventually go into the Batmobile, but for the time being, it just has an old 87 truck 350 motor that is bone stock (except for the Edelbrock Performer carb) with lots of miles. It used a 1/2 quart of oil on my 400 mile road trip. Admittedly, I was playing around and driving fast, but it's tired. Still lots of fun though! Twice the displacement of the 2.8 V6. I'm guessing this engine the Batmobile currently has, is about 200 to 220 hp and about 300 ft/lbs of torque at best. Maybe less since it needs rebuilt. Look at the torque numbers, not the horsepower. The new hipo engine I'm building should have close to 450 ft/lbs of torque! Awesome!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 05-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||frontal lobe||05-23-2000||02:21 AM||||I got to go to a piano recital at a nursing home and mow the lawn.  Quite a contrast in weekends!  Glad you were feeling up to it and had a great time.||||reg||1
Z||000010||frontal lobe||05-23-2000||02:22 AM||||Oh yeah.  Was going to ask.  What kind of range did you get between fill-ups?||||reg||1
Z||000011||batboy||05-23-2000||09:30 AM||||I didn't check mileage, but I will say this, it seemed like I stopped for gas a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DJRice||05-23-2000||09:43 AM||||Holy Mid-engined marvel, batboy!  The batmobile is looking good.  When you get that z28 motor in there, I'll probably be able to hear you light the tires up all the way down here in FL.<P>"a kansas wheat field"??<P>I thought kansas was <B><I>the</B></I> wheat field..Hehe<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Raydar||05-23-2000||09:44 AM||||What's that sucking sound that I hear?<BR>(...as the gas tank implodes upon itself.)<BR>J/K!!!<P>Congrats! Looks great. Heckuva sleeper. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||kevin||05-23-2000||10:09 AM||||I think your car looks terrific. I would be cautious in over modifying the body. I would say that a overdone body with add-ons, geek-ahs, lowrider paint, etc looks the same as the ignorant slob in the year 2000 who still believes that wearing platform shoes, a razor blade necklace and puka-shells makes him "big daddy" at the disco.<BR>I am just advising you not to get too carried away. Follow the dictum of the other great supercars: 'less is more'. I really enjoy your car. It looks all the world like mine. I need to know, do you have a 5-speed or auto? Any chassis mods? Lets keep this thread going. You inspire alot of people batman.||||reg||1
Z||000015||batboy||05-23-2000||10:32 AM||||Kevin, don't worry about me overdoing it. Everything except possibly the rear wing is being added for pure functionality. It does have an automatic tranny. You ask if they are any chassis mods? The entire suspension and steering has either been rebuilt or upgraded. Two inch drop all the way around, rear coil-overs, poly bushings, new everything.||||reg||1
Z||000016||bHooper||05-23-2000||10:35 AM||||Batboy... Congrats!  I share your enthusiasm.  Although, just being able to drive my car whenever I feel like it will make me satisfied!<P>Enjoy!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000017||Phil||05-23-2000||11:17 AM||||How does the bump steer kit feel so far notice any difference?||||reg||1
Z||000018||batboy||05-23-2000||02:21 PM||||Phil, to be perfectly honest, I don't know. The ride and handling is tremedously improved from before, but is it because of the poly bushings, or the new tie rods and ball joints, or the bump steering correction kit, or the rear coil-overs, or a combination of all of the above, I don't really know. I suspect a combination of everything. I do know the tires are the weak point now. Gotta save some dough for new tires.||||reg||1
